        # This corresponds to b=1 in the problem statement? 
        # The problem says: "For every nonnegative integer b, block b contains ... 10*b through 10*b+9".
        # And "If b is odd, append decreasing". 
        # The sequence given: 1-9, then 19-10 (which is 10-19 reversed), then 20-29, then 39-30 (30-39 reversed).
        # So:
        # After 1-9, we have block b=1 (odd): 10*1=10 to 19. Decreasing: 19,18,...,10.
        # Then block b=2 (even): 20 to 29. Increasing: 20,21,...,29.
        # Then block b=3 (odd): 30 to 39. Decreasing: 39,38,...,30.
        
        # So the blocks of 2-digit numbers start from b=1.
